-- Rules of Court 2021 (Singapore), G.N. No. S 914/2021, current version as at 5 November 2026.
-- ORDER 22 (ENFORCEMENT OF JUDGMENTS AND ORDERS), rules 10 to 13: claims and objections to seizure or attachment,
-- examination of the enforcement respondent, instalment payments, stay of enforcement.
-- Rules 1 to 5 are in roc5-o22-order.l4 and rules 6 to 9 in roc5-o22-sheriff.l4.  LAYER 1: the law, objectively.
-- Source: a plain-text rendering made by a converter script from Singapore Statutes Online.
-- It is not the official text, and nothing here has been checked against the official text.
--
-- HOW TO READ A RESULT: as in roc5-o20.l4.  JUST TRUE and JUST FALSE are the text's own yes and no;
-- NOTHING is "not covered"; a caller must never turn NOTHING into FALSE.
-- Rule 10 is also written as regulative rules (PARTY ... MUST ... WITHIN ... LEST ...), run by #TRACE.  A regulative
-- rule counts a plain number of days from the moment the trace starts; the decision function beside it counts the
-- period by Order 3 rule 3 (an input) and is the one the layer 2 questions use.
-- Seam S-L2: nothing here asks whether the Government is a party (Order 59 rule 11 switches Order 22 off for the
-- Government, in another part).  "Subject to any written law" is not threaded as an input (NOTES.md).

-- ===========================================================================
§ `Order 22, rules 10 to 13 -- objections, examination, instalments, stay`
-- ===========================================================================

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
§§ `Rule 10 -- claims and objections to seizure or attachment`
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

`o 22 r 10(1) the period for filing and serving the notice of objection` MEANS Period WITH
    `period length` IS 14
    `period unit` IS Days
    `period direction` IS `After the anchor`

-- (1)(a): "Where the enforcement respondent or any other person objects ... to any seizure of property or attachment
-- of a debt by the Sheriff, the objector must within 14 days after the service of the notice of seizure or attachment".
-- src:3530 | 10. —(1) Where the enforcement respondent or any other person objects (each called in this Rule the objector) to any seizure of property or attachment of a debt by the Sheriff, the objector must within 14 days after the service of the notice of seizure or attachment — ( a )
-- src:3531 | give notice of such objection to the Sheriff by filing a notice of objection; and
@ref O 22 r 10(1)(a) (src:3530-3531)
GIVEN `the person objects to a seizure of property or an attachment of a debt by the Sheriff` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the date the notice of objection is filed with the Sheriff` IS A DATE
      `o 3 r 3 the last day for doing the act` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 22 r 10(1)(a) the objector gives notice of the objection to the Sheriff in time` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the person objects to a seizure of property or an attachment of a debt by the Sheriff`
        THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where the enforcement respondent or any other person objects (each called in this Rule the objector) to any seizure of property or attachment of a debt by the Sheriff" [where, ruled 2026-11-05 (b)]
        IF `the date the notice of objection is filed with the Sheriff` AT MOST `o 3 r 3 the last day for doing the act`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "within 14 days after the service of the notice of seizure or attachment" [period, ruled 2026-11-05 (a)]

