    PARTY `o 22 r 10 the objector` DOES `o 22 r 10(1)(b) serves a copy of the notice of objection on the persons the rule names` AT 15

-- No act at all: the clock reaches day 15 and the duty of the objector is breached by expiry.
#TRACE `o 22 r 10(1) the duty of the objector` AT 0 WITH
    (WAITUNTIL 15)

-- (2): the contents of the notice.
-- src:3534 | (2) The notice of objection must identify the objector, specify the property or debt in dispute, state the grounds of objection and include any evidence supporting the grounds of objection.
@ref O 22 r 10(2) (src:3534-3534)
GIVEN `the notice identifies the objector` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the notice specifies the property or debt in dispute` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the notice states the grounds of objection` IS A BOOLEAN
      `there is evidence supporting the grounds of objection` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the notice includes the evidence supporting the grounds of objection` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 22 r 10(2) the notice of objection has the contents the rule requires` MEANS
    IF `the notice identifies the objector`
       AND `the notice specifies the property or debt in dispute`
       AND `the notice states the grounds of objection`
       AND ((NOT `there is evidence supporting the grounds of objection`) OR `the notice includes the evidence supporting the grounds of objection`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The notice of objection must identify the objector, specify the property or debt in dispute, state the grounds of objection and include any evidence supporting the grounds of objection"

