-- (4): the Sheriff may direct the objector to apply to the Court if, within 14 days, the applicant fails to consent
-- or gives notice of dispute.
-- src:3536 | (4) If the enforcement applicant, within 14 days after the service of the notice of objection, fails to consent to the release or gives notice of dispute, the Sheriff may direct the objector to apply to the Court for an order to release the specified property or debt.
