      `the enforcement applicant gave notice of dispute within the 14 days` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the 14 days after the service of the notice of objection have passed` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 22 r 10(4) the Sheriff may direct the objector to apply to the Court` MEANS
    IF `the enforcement applicant gave notice of dispute within the 14 days` OR (`the 14 days after the service of the notice of objection have passed` AND (NOT `the enforcement applicant consented to the release within the 14 days after the service of the notice of objection`))
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If the enforcement applicant, within 14 days after the service of the notice of objection, fails to consent to the release or gives notice of dispute, the Sheriff may direct the objector to apply to the Court" [if, marginal reading (a)]

