§§ `Rule 11 -- examination of the enforcement respondent`
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- src:3547 | 11. —(1) The enforcement applicant may apply for the enforcement respondent to be examined orally in court or to make an affidavit or both on the properties which are owned by the enforcement respondent beneficially whether in whole or in part or which the enforcement respondent will be entitled to in the future. (2) The Court may also order the enforcement respondent to produce such documents as are appropriate.
@ref O 22 r 11(1) (src:3547-3547)
GIVEN `the person is an enforcement applicant` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the properties are owned by the enforcement respondent beneficially, whether in whole or in part` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the enforcement respondent will be entitled to the properties in the future` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 22 r 11(1) the enforcement applicant may apply for the enforcement respondent to be examined orally in court or to make an affidavit or both on the properties` MEANS
    IF `the person is an enforcement applicant` AND (`the properties are owned by the enforcement respondent beneficially, whether in whole or in part` OR `the enforcement respondent will be entitled to the properties in the future`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "on the properties which are owned by the enforcement respondent beneficially whether in whole or in part or which the enforcement respondent will be entitled to in the future"

-- src:3547 | 11. —(1) The enforcement applicant may apply for the enforcement respondent to be examined orally in court or to make an affidavit or both on the properties which are owned by the enforcement respondent beneficially whether in whole or in part or which the enforcement respondent will be entitled to in the future. (2) The Court may also order the enforcement respondent to produce such documents as are appropriate.
@ref O 22 r 11(2) (src:3547-3547)
GIVEN `the documents are appropriate` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 22 r 11(2) the Court may order the enforcement respondent to produce the documents` MEANS
    IF `the documents are appropriate`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "such documents as are appropriate"

