-- src:3550 | (5) An order under this Rule must be in Form 41 and must be served personally on the enforcement respondent and, where the enforcement respondent is an entity, on any officer of the entity ordered to attend for examination.
@ref O 22 r 11(5) (src:3550-3550)
GIVEN `it is an order under Rule 11` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the order is in Form 41` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the order is served personally on the enforcement respondent` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the enforcement respondent is an entity` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the order is served personally on any officer of the entity ordered to attend for examination` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 22 r 11(5) the order is made and served as the rule requires` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `it is an order under Rule 11`
        THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "An order under this Rule"
        IF `the order is in Form 41` AND `the order is served personally on the enforcement respondent` AND ((NOT `the enforcement respondent is an entity`) OR `the order is served personally on any officer of the entity ordered to attend for examination`)
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "An order under this Rule must be in Form 41 and must be served personally on the enforcement respondent and, where the enforcement respondent is an entity, on any officer of the entity ordered to attend for examination"

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
§§ `Rule 12 -- instalment payments`
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- "Where" governs the instalment-order clause only.  "that is due and unpaid" is a relative clause that says
-- which instalments the applicant may apply for; it is not a "where", and it is not an "only" either, so an
-- instalment that is not yet due is left unanswered (ruling (c) of 2026-11-05; fork F10).
-- src:3552 | 12. Where a Court order made under section 43 of the State Courts Act or under any other written law provides for payment by instalments, the enforcement applicant may apply for an enforcement order in respect of an instalment that is due and unpaid or, if there are several instalments due and unpaid, in respect of those instalments.
@ref O 22 r 12 (src:3552-3552)
GIVEN `a Court order made under section 43 of the State Courts Act or under any other written law provides for payment by instalments` IS A BOOLEAN
      `an instalment is due and unpaid` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 22 r 12 the enforcement applicant may apply for an enforcement order in respect of the instalments due and unpaid` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `a Court order made under section 43 of the State Courts Act or under any other written law provides for payment by instalments`
        THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where a Court order made under section 43 of the State Courts Act or under any other written law provides for payment by instalments, the enforcement applicant may apply for an enforcement order in respect of an instalment that is due and unpaid" [where, ruled 2026-11-05 (b)]
        IF `an instalment is due and unpaid`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "in respect of an instalment that is due and unpaid" is a relative clause, not a "where", and has no "only" [scope limit, ruled 2026-11-05 (c)]

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
§§ `Rule 13 -- application for stay of enforcement`
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- src:3554 | 13. —(1) The party who is liable under any Court order may apply for stay of enforcement or stay of any enforcement order or any part of the order if there is a special case making it inappropriate to enforce the Court order immediately. (2) The Court may order a stay of enforcement or stay of an enforcement order, for a specified period or until the occurrence of a specified event.
@ref O 22 r 13(1) (src:3554-3554)
GIVEN `the party is liable under a Court order` IS A BOOLEAN
      `there is a special case making it inappropriate to enforce the Court order immediately` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 22 r 13(1) the party may apply for stay of enforcement or stay of the enforcement order` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the party is liable under a Court order`
        THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "The party who is liable under any Court order"
        IF `there is a special case making it inappropriate to enforce the Court order immediately`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "if there is a special case making it inappropriate to enforce the Court order immediately" [if, marginal reading (a)]

DECLARE `o 22 r 13(2) how long the stay lasts` IS ONE OF
    `o 22 r 13(2) for a specified period`
    `o 22 r 13(2) until the occurrence of a specified event`
    `o 22 r 13(2) in some other way`

-- src:3554 | 13. —(1) The party who is liable under any Court order may apply for stay of enforcement or stay of any enforcement order or any part of the order if there is a special case making it inappropriate to enforce the Court order immediately. (2) The Court may order a stay of enforcement or stay of an enforcement order, for a specified period or until the occurrence of a specified event.
@ref O 22 r 13(2) (src:3554-3554)
GIVEN duration IS A `o 22 r 13(2) how long the stay lasts`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 22 r 13(2) the Court may order a stay of enforcement or of an enforcement order for the duration` MEANS
    CONSIDER duration
    WHEN `o 22 r 13(2) for a specified period` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `o 22 r 13(2) until the occurrence of a specified event` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `o 22 r 13(2) in some other way` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "for a specified period or until the occurrence of a specified event"

DECLARE `o 22 r 13(3) direction to the Sheriff` IS ONE OF
    `o 22 r 13(3) to withdraw the seizure or attachment`
    `o 22 r 13(3) to maintain the seizure or attachment without taking further action on the enforcement order`
    `o 22 r 13(3) some other direction`

-- src:3555 | (3) Where the Sheriff has seized properties or attached a debt under the enforcement order before the Court orders a stay, the order may give directions to the Sheriff to withdraw the seizure or attachment or to maintain the seizure or attachment without taking further action on the enforcement order.
@ref O 22 r 13(3) (src:3555-3555)
GIVEN direction IS A `o 22 r 13(3) direction to the Sheriff`
      `the Sheriff has seized properties or attached a debt under the enforcement order before the Court orders a stay` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 22 r 13(3) the order may give the direction to the Sheriff` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the Sheriff has seized properties or attached a debt under the enforcement order before the Court orders a stay`
        THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where the Sheriff has seized properties or attached a debt under the enforcement order before the Court orders a stay" [where, ruled 2026-11-05 (b)]
        IF direction EQUALS `o 22 r 13(3) some other direction`
        THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "the order may give directions to the Sheriff to withdraw the seizure or attachment or to maintain the seizure or attachment without taking further action on the enforcement order"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE
